+// Request only the scopes the Feishu app has enabled as user-authorized
+// permissions. Deriving the OAuth scope list from every action's
+// providerPermissions requests permissions the app has not enabled
+// (e.g. slash command / approval), and Feishu's authorize endpoint then
+// rejects the whole request with error 20027 before the user can even see
+// the consent page. Missing action-level permissions surface as runtime
+// errors instead, which keeps the authorization entry working.
+// The whitelist must stay a subset of the app's enabled user-authorized
+// permissions — extend the console first, then this list. Beyond the
+// foundational set in scopes.ts it covers the document import chain
+// (drive listing, wiki tree, search, comments).
